<!--
  Step 1 of the per-traveller release.

  The new object, its fields, the two permission sets and the guest sharing rule
  that belongs to the object. No Apex, so production runs no tests and nothing
  can fail on access to fields nobody has been granted yet.

  Nothing in production reads or writes this object until step 3 deploys the
  Apex, so this is additive and inert on its own.

  Between this and step 3, Golf_Extra_Feedback_Admin has to be assigned to the
  people who should see invitations, including whoever runs the next deploy.
  That assignment is what the failing validation was missing.
-->
